Interview Questions
What is Linux?

Linux is an open-source operating system kernel used as the foundation for many Linux distributions.

What is the difference between / and /root?

/ is the root of the Linux filesystem, while /root is the home directory of the root user.

What is the difference between an absolute and relative path?

An absolute path starts from / and specifies the complete location. A relative path specifies a location relative to the current working directory.
